title: "gradinv: algebra, closed-form compliance and orientation averages of cubic and hexagonal strain-gradient elasticity tensors"
authors:
  - family-names: "González-Monsalve"
    given-names: "Daniel"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3892-4722"
    affiliation: "Department of Mechanical Engineering, Faculty of Engineering, Universidad de Concepción, Concepción, Chile"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-16"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24267836"
    description: "Version 1.0.0 archived at Zenodo"
abstract: >-
  Code and data for the article "Algebra, closed-form compliance and orientation
  averages of cubic and hexagonal strain-gradient elasticity tensors". The Python
  package gradinv builds coordinate-free bases, with closed multiplication tables, of
  the algebras of sixth-order tensors of Mindlin's strain-gradient elasticity (form II)
  for the cubic class m-3m and the hexagonal class 6/mmm, and with them computes
  products, inverses, Voigt, Reuss and Hill orientation averages and concentration
  tensors on small blocks. The repository also contains the scripts that write every
  table, figure and computed number of the article and its supplementary material, the
  input data with the provenance of every number, and the test suite.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/daniel-gonzalezm/gradinv"
keywords:
  - strain-gradient elasticity
  - sixth-order tensors
  - cubic and hexagonal symmetry
  - tensor algebra
  - orientation averages
  - polycrystals
